   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_14"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "How did I get sunburned on a cloudy, windy hike?",
   "est_sec": 3.2,
   "gap_before": 0.21,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "hiking.dlg28"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Clouds don't block much UV, and wind cools your skin so you don't feel yourself burning.",
   "est_sec": 5.06,
   "gap_before": 0.7,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "hiking.dlg28"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Hold on, can you say that again?",
   "est_sec": 2.27,
   "gap_before": 3.15,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "kind": "wait_like",
   "phrasing": "waitlike_02",
   "block": "hiking.dlg28"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "No problem. Clouds don't block much UV, and wind cools your skin so you don't feel yourself burning.",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 1.7,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "hiking.dlg28"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "That's sneaky.",
   "est_sec": 0.72,
   "gap_before": 0.79,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "hiking.dlg28"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "It really is. Higher up, the sun is also stronger than at sea level.",
   "est_sec": 4.44,
   "gap_before": 1.73,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "hiking.dlg28"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "So sunscreen even in April.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 1.27,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "hiking.dlg28"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Yes, and reapply it after a couple of hours or if you sweat a lot. Don't forget your ears and the back of your neck.",
   "est_sec": 7.85,
   "gap_before": 0.65,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "hiking.dlg28"
  },
  {
